  "notes": "Announced in the Phi-3.5 post of 2024-08-22; the model card gives Release date: August 2024. Sources disagree on the language model inside: the model card says it contains the Phi-3 Mini language model, while the Phi-3 technical report v4 says its decoder is phi-3.5-mini and calls it derived from phi-3.5-mini; no derived-from relation is recorded until this is settled. Image encoder CLIP ViT-L/14 from OpenAI per the report (cross-organisation component). Listed on the Retired Microsoft Foundry Models page (retired 2025-08-30), so it was offered in Foundry; the sources do not describe a serverless API, so api is not recorded. Microsoft reported benchmark results."
